      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "East Asian individuals are often stereotyped as being more stoic and resilient under pressure, sometimes exhibiting a tendency towards internalizing stress. Mediterranean temperaments, in contrast, are frequently characterized by more overt emotional expression and a tendency towards externalizing stress responses when faced with high-stress situations. These generalizations, however, are broad and do not account for individual variation within any ethnic group. It's important to note that cultural norms heavily influence how stress is perceived and displayed, rather than inherent biological differences.",
